    "abstract": "Parts breakdown of the forward engine mount side link fitting installation, showing the bonded-bush and the interference-fit fitting standards as a life-limited item pair with the attachment bolts catalogued separately.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure gives the parts breakdown of the forward engine mount side link fitting installation on the pylon primary structure.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the left-hand pylon looking inboard; the right-hand pylon is symmetrically opposite. Items 10 and 10A are the two fitting standards and the pylon is drilled to one or the other, so a change of standard cannot be reversed. Both are life-limited parts: the item carries the life record and the cycle count must travel with the part, which is why the fitting is no longer catalogued together with its attachment set. The attachment bolts are now item 80 and are orderable on their own, so that a fitting can be reinstalled on another aircraft without ordering a fitting to get the bolts."
    },
