    "abstract": "Parts breakdown of the forward engine mount side link fitting installation, showing the three fitting standards under a three-way effectivity together with the interface plate, the additional cleat and the bolt set that change with the four-bolt standard.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure gives the parts breakdown of the forward engine mount side link fitting installation on the pylon primary structure.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the left-hand pylon looking inboard; the right-hand pylon is symmetrically opposite. Sheet 2 shows the four-bolt pattern. Items 10, 10A and 10B are the three fitting standards and the pylon is drilled to one of them, so no change of standard can be reversed. All three are life-limited parts and the cycle count travels with the item. The interface plate is not common across the effectivity: item 50 is the three-bolt plate and item 50A the four-bolt plate, and the bolt set follows in the same way at items 80 and 80A. The cleat at item 40 exists only on the four-bolt standard. Do not order item 50A against a fitting at item 10 or 10A; the hole pattern will not line up and the plate cannot be reworked."
    },
